  "rationale": "Both answers are valid and the English cue/sense is aligned. However, the national split is materially overstated: Indonesian official banking usage also uses \"pemegang rekening,\" while Malaysian banking usage also uses \"pemilik akaun.\" The relation should reflect shared accepted synonyms or a non-exclusive preference, not an unqualified different-common-word contrast. No genuine false-friend contrast is supported.",
